// Log F1 (docs/verification/miscompile-log.md). The parser recurses once per
// nesting level with no limit, so a deeply nested expression kills the
// compiler with a stack overflow (exit 0xC00000FD, "Stack overflow: the
// recursion is too deep") instead of compiling it or reporting "nested too
// deeply". 3000 parentheses here; any of ( [ { - ! does it. Found by
// scripts/fuzz/fuzz_frontend.py (VF3).
// The fix (Nov 17) is a limit: 256 levels, then "nested too deeply" with
// the place (tests/bootstrap/test_verify_parser_nesting_limit_fail.fd,
// test_verify_parser_nesting_ok.fd), so this program is rejected, not run.
//! error: nested too deeply

